# Keep derived TagSession state in sync with tags

## Game-time phase and period labels

`TagSession` quarter phase, current quarter, start-anchor time, **and closed Q1–Q4 spans** are derived from the **game-time index** (`gameTimeTags_`: start-anchor + Q1–Q4 only) in `restoreGameTimeStateFromTags()`. Timeouts are not in that index.

Call restore after the index changes: adding/removing/retiming a start-anchor or quarter tag, or after `importTags` / `clear`. Do **not** restore after ordinary play-tag add/remove/trim — that was a full scan of every tag.

`periodLabelAtTimestampMs()` only **reads** `closedQuarters_` / phase (O(4)). Do not walk or sort `tags_` on every label lookup, and do not keep a second quarter parser.

Keep `gameTimeTags_` in `tags_` order. Last duplicate quarter in that order wins (same as a full scan). Rebuild the index from `tags_` after import/sort; incremental upsert/remove by tag id on single-tag edits.

Phase follows the contiguous closed prefix Q1..Qn (a missing Q2 does not skip to Q3 or end the game). Labels must still work when:

- Q1 is in progress and no quarter tag is closed yet (`currentQuarterIndex_` + `currentQuarterStartMs_`)
- the game has ended and the timestamp is after Q4’s recorded end (still Q4)

`GameEnded` does **not** set `currentQuarterIndex_` to 3. That index means “quarter in progress”; leaving it at -1 prevents `onNextQuarterRequested` from closing Q4 twice. `periodLabelAtTimestampMs` uses `closedQuarters_[Q4]` for in-span and post-end timestamps. Tagging UI (`contextPeriod_`) must map `GameEnded` to Q4 itself — do not read `currentQuarterIndex()` as the period after the whistle.

```cpp
// BAD — rebuild/sort closed quarters on every playhead query
QString TagSession::periodLabelAtTimestampMs(qint64 positionMs) const {
  return periodLabelFromSnapshot(collectGameTimeFromTags(tags_), positionMs);
}

// BAD — restore scans every play tag on Goal add / clip trim
void TagSession::addTag(const GameTag& tag) {
  tags_.push_back(tag);
  restoreGameTimeStateFromTags();  // walked tags_
}

// GOOD — restore fills closedQuarters_ / phase from gameTimeTags_; labels read members only
void TagSession::restoreGameTimeStateFromTags();  // walks gameTimeTags_ (typically ≤ 5)
QString TagSession::periodLabelAtTimestampMs(qint64 positionMs) const;  // reads closedQuarters_
```

## Event counts

`mainEventCounts_` and `followUpCountsByMainEvent_` are derived in `rebuildEventCountsFromTags()`. Call it after any path that adds or removes tags (`addTag`, `removeTag`, `importTags`, `clear`). Do not increment/decrement counts manually in mutation handlers — one missed path desynchronizes filters and presentation UI.

```cpp
// BAD — manual +/- in addTag/removeTag plus full rebuild elsewhere
mainEventCounts_.insert(stored.mainEvent, mainEventCounts_.value(stored.mainEvent, 0) + 1);

// GOOD — single rebuild from tags_
tags_.push_back(stored);
rebuildEventCountsFromTags();
restoreGameTimeStateFromTags();
```

Listeners (`restoreGamePhase`) must run on `tagsChanged`, not only on `tagsImported`.
